  AgentDecisionLog append-only decision commitments
    [32m√[39m only the owner registers immutable versions and role permissions
    [32m√[39m rejects empty version metadata, zero role addresses and unknown versions
    [32m√[39m requires the explicit anchorer role, including for the owner, and permits revocation
    [32m√[39m commits exact continuous ranges and events without duplicate or skipped sequences
    [32m√[39m rejects empty roots, mismatched counts, reversed ranges and batches over 256 (59ms)
    [32m√[39m verifies JavaScript-generated proofs on the real local contract (1 leaves)
    [32m√[39m verifies JavaScript-generated proofs on the real local contract (3 leaves)
    [32m√[39m verifies JavaScript-generated proofs on the real local contract (256 leaves) (40ms)
    [32m√[39m ownership transfer preserves batch history and does not implicitly grant the new owner an anchorer role
    [32m√[39m deployment defaults to zero broadcasts and needs no signer, network, keys or filesystem
    [32m√[39m deploys and initializes locally, merges only the new contract, verifies bytecode and resumes without retransmission (52ms)

  RWAOfferingPool hardening
    collateral: one eBL backs one live offering
      [32m√[39m refuses a second offering on an eBL that already backs a live one
      [32m√[39m frees the eBL when an unsubscribed offering is cancelled, so it can be offered again (47ms)
      [32m√[39m releases the pledge when an offering is repaid, so the eBL can move again
      1) still settles when the registry owner already released the pledge, and reports it
      2) stops selling shares once the eBL is no longer pledged to the pool
    pricing bounds
      [32m√[39m never lets the oracle price an offering above its target redemption value
      3) REPRICE_DOWN has to lower the price
      4) allows a recovery: an OPEN action may raise a repriced offering again, up to the target
      [32m√[39m rejects an out-of-range risk level at the oracle and a zero pool
    settlement
      [32m√[39m refuses proofs and settlement for an offering nobody subscribed to
      [32m√[39m lets only the owner correct a mistaken importer payment, and keeps the audit trail
      [32m√[39m validates a correction
      [32m√[39m records the departure proof and the oracle / token wiring in the event log
    cancelOffering
      [32m√[39m is owner-only and needs an existing offering
      [32m√[39m cannot cancel an offering that already has subscribers
      5) works from Open, Repriced and Paused, also during a global emergency stop
      [32m√[39m rejects a second cancel and any state that is not cancellable
    documented limitation
      [32m√[39m subscribe records an amount owed but holds no funds (no payment leg yet)

  EBLRegistry hardening
    [32m√[39m registers a legacy document only once, whoever holds it
    [32m√[39m only the owner can register eBLs, and a V2 cargo hash can never be registered twice
    6) only the holder can transfer or endorse, never while pledged, and never to a bad recipient

  PaymentOracle ownership
    [32m√[39m hands the contract over in two steps and moves the attestor role with it
    [32m√[39m keeps an explicitly authorised attestor across an ownership transfer

  two-step ownership of the protocol contracts
    [32m√[39m registry: a transfer completes only when the nominee accepts
    [32m√[39m token: a transfer completes only when the nominee accepts (38ms)
    [32m√[39m pool: a transfer completes only when the nominee accepts (46ms)
    [32m√[39m oracle: a transfer completes only when the nominee accepts
    [32m√[39m gate: a transfer completes only when the nominee accepts (41ms)
    [32m√[39m a nomination can be replaced before it is accepted (41ms)
    [32m√[39m the new pool owner takes over the administrative powers
    [32m√[39m the oracle updater role moves with ownership, like the deployer role it started as (48ms)

